  "result": "Shell completion now keeps `#` as an ordinary character in an argument. Before, it dropped everything after the `#`. The tests in `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (68 passed).\n\n- **Fix:** in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), I set `lex.commenters = \"\"`, so `cli a#b c` now splits into `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`.\n- **Tests:** I added three cases to `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b` mid-line, a leading `#a`, and `'a#b` with a missing closing quote.\n- **Changelog:** I added an \"Unreleased\" entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
